$ whycant -u root read /root/.ssh/id_ed25519

? could not determine whether root (uid 0) can read /root/.ssh/id_ed25519

  /                       drwxr-xr-x  root:root  ✓ traverse
  /root                   drwx------  root:root  ✓ traverse
  /root/.ssh              ·                      ? cannot inspect   ← cannot see past here
  /root/.ssh/id_ed25519   ·           not evaluated

Why
  whycant is running as alice and is not allowed to look at /root/.ssh,
  so it cannot tell what lies beyond it.

Fixes (safest first)
  1. Run whycant as root to see the whole chain:
       sudo whycant -u root read /root/.ssh/id_ed25519
